// A type-checker for a meaningful subset of VL, written in VL — the stage between the
// parser and the emitter. It consumes the parser's node arena (`P.nodes`) directly: it
// lexes nothing and parses nothing itself. Checker state lives in the global `T`, like
// the parser's `P`.
//
// A `type` union alias cannot self- or forward-reference its own members, so a recursive
// `VLType` is not expressible in VL. Types live in a flat arena `T.tys: Ty[]` and every
// place a type would nest another holds an `i32` index into it (`TyObj.objFieldTypes`,
// `TyFunc.fnRet`, `TyUnion.uMembers`, `TyNullable.nInner`) — the AST node arena's own
// workaround, applied to the type algebra. The visitor is factored: per-kind helpers
// (`checkCallNode`, `checkFuncDeclNode`, `checkProgramNode`) take the narrowed variant
// as a struct parameter and recurse back through `checkNode`.

